:: NPC offer soda - spray reaction
<<set _goodwillDelta = _goodwillDelta ?? 0>>
<<set _goodwillPart = _goodwillDelta ? ' &bull; Goodwill ' + (_goodwillDelta >= 0 ? '+' : '') + _goodwillDelta : ''>>
<<set _reactionPct = _mcJoined ? 100 : ($tmpGirl.relationship + (_sodaLikedByNpc ? 10 : 0))>>
<<set _reactionPositive = _mcJoined || setup.percentageChance(_reactionPct)>>

<<if _reactionPositive>>
	<<if _mcJoined>>
		<<set _reactHappy = 1>>
		<<set _reactRel = 2>>
		<<set _reactSub = -3>>
		<<set _preSprayJoinSub = $tmpGirl.sub>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.happy = Math.min($tmpGirl.happy + 1, 100)>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.relationship = Math.min($tmpGirl.relationship + 2, 100)>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.sub = Math.max($tmpGirl.sub - 3, 0)>>
		<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> stares at you a second, soda dripping down your front, then breaks into laughter so hard <<=_heOrShe>> nearly drops <<=_hisOrHer>> own can. Whatever this was supposed to be, you've turned it into something the two of you did together instead of something done to <<=_himOrHer>>.
		<br /><br />
		<<if _preSprayJoinSub < 20>>
			<<set _joinLines = [
				"Ha! Serves you right. Now we're even.",
				"Good. Now you know how it feels.",
				"Well, look at that — you're just as much of a mess as me now, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + ".",
				"Guess karma didn't waste any time with you, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + "."
			]>>
		<<elseif _preSprayJoinSub < 50>>
			<<set _joinLines = [
				"Okay, that's actually kind of adorable. Didn't expect that side of you.",
				"That's surprisingly charming, watching you make a fool of yourself for me.",
				"I like this side of you, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + ". Didn't know you had it in you.",
				"You're kind of a dork, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + ". I mean that as a compliment."
			]>>
		<<elseif _preSprayJoinSub <= 90>>
			<<set _joinLines = [
				"You really didn't need to do that — someone who runs this whole place shouldn't be covered in soda over something so small.",
				"It just feels wrong, seeing you like this. You've got enough weighing on you without adding 'sticky' to the list.",
				"That's not something you should have to deal with, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + ". You've got bigger things to worry about than soda.",
				"Someone like you shouldn't be dealing with this kind of mess, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + ". But... thank you, I guess."
			]>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _joinLines = [
				"It's sweet, I guess. Just — you shouldn't have to get messy over someone like me.",
				"That's... funny, actually. Though it feels strange, seeing you like this. For my sake.",
				"You didn't have to lower yourself like that for me, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + "... but thank you.",
				"I appreciate it, truly. But someone like you shouldn't be covered in soda because of me, " + setup.npc.mcName($tmpGirl) + "."
			]>>
		<</if>>
		<<sayNpc $tmpGirl>><<=setup.getRandomElement(_joinLines)>><</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _attractedToMC>>
		<<set _reactHappy = 1>>
		<<set _reactRel = 0>>
		<<set _reactSub = 2>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.happy = Math.min($tmpGirl.happy + 1, 100)>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.sub = Math.min($tmpGirl.sub + 2, 100)>>
		<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> yelps, then laughs, soda soaking through the front of <<=_hisOrHer>> top as <<=_heOrShe>> wipes <<=_hisOrHer>> face with the back of <<=_hisOrHer>> hand, eyes finding yours through it.
	<<else>>
		<<set _reactHappy = 1>>
		<<set _reactRel = 0>>
		<<set _reactSub = 1>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.happy = Math.min($tmpGirl.happy + 1, 100)>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.sub = Math.min($tmpGirl.sub + 1, 100)>>
		<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> yelps, then laughs despite <<=_himOrHer>>self, soda soaking through <<=_hisOrHer>> clothes.
	<</if>>
	<br />
	<<if _attractedToMC>>
		<<=ucfirst(_hisOrHer)>> top clings wet against <<=_himOrHer>>, and as <<=_heOrShe>> plucks at the soaked fabric, grumbling about needing to get cleaned up, you find your eyes lingering on it a little too long — and an idea starts to form.
		<br /><br />
		<<set _showerLinkText = 'Take ' + _himOrHer + ' to the shower'>>
		<div id="btn_spray_shower_choice">
			<<linkreplace `_showerLinkText`>>
				<<run $('#btn_spray_send_off').hide()>>
				You nod toward the house, and <<=_heOrShe>> follows without needing to be asked twice, peeling the sticky shirt away from <<=_hisOrHer>> skin as you go.
				<br /><br />
				<<link 'Continue'>>
					<<set $oldTmpGirlLocation = $tmpGirl.location>>
					<<set $tmpGirl.location = 'shower'>>
					<<set $tmpGirlViewBack = _backPassage>>
					<<fuck $tmpGirl>>
				<</link>>
			<</linkreplace>>
		</div>
		<<set _sendOffLinkText = 'Send ' + _himOrHer + ' to clean up'>>
		<div id="btn_spray_send_off">
			<<link `_sendOffLinkText`>>
				<<set $tmpGirl.rest = { days: 1, desc: 'Cleaning up after a soda mishap', id: 'resting' }>>
				<<goto _backPassage>>
			<</link>>
		</div>
		<div class="link-desc">Happiness +<<=_reactHappy>><<if _reactRel>> &bull; Relationship +<<=_reactRel>><</if>> &bull; Submission <<=(_reactSub >= 0 ? '+' : '') + _reactSub>><<=_goodwillPart>> (either option)</div>
	<<elseif $tmpGirl.location === 'milk_barn'>>
		Sticky and a mess now, <<=_heOrShe>> looks down at <<=_himOrHer>>self, soda dripping off the tubing, somewhere between amused and annoyed as <<=_heOrShe>> mutters a "thanks" for the gesture and waits to see what you'll decide.
		<br /><br />
		<div id="btn_spray_milkbarn">
			<<link 'Let her disconnect and clean up'>>
				<<set $tmpGirl.happy = Math.min($tmpGirl.happy + 1, 100)>>
				<<set $tmpGirl.rest = { days: 1, desc: 'Cleaning up after a soda mishap', id: 'resting' }>>
				<<goto _backPassage>>
			<</link>>
			<div class="link-desc">Happiness <<=((_reactHappy + 1) >= 0 ? '+' : '') + (_reactHappy + 1)>><<if _reactRel>> &bull; Relationship +<<=_reactRel>><</if>> &bull; Submission <<=(_reactSub >= 0 ? '+' : '') + _reactSub>><<=_goodwillPart>></div>
			<br />
			<<link 'Make her finish the workday sticky'>>
				<<set $tmpGirl.happy = Math.max($tmpGirl.happy - 2, -100)>>
				<<set $tmpGirl.sub = Math.min($tmpGirl.sub + 1, 100)>>
				<<goto _backPassage>>
			<</link>>
			<div class="link-desc">Happiness <<=((_reactHappy - 2) >= 0 ? '+' : '') + (_reactHappy - 2)>><<if _reactRel>> &bull; Relationship +<<=_reactRel>><</if>> &bull; Submission <<=((_reactSub + 1) >= 0 ? '+' : '') + (_reactSub + 1)>><<=_goodwillPart>></div>
		</div>
	<<else>>
		<<set $tmpGirl.rest = { days: 1, desc: 'Cleaning up after a soda mishap', id: 'resting' }>>
		Sticky and a mess now, somewhere between amused and annoyed, <<=_heOrShe>> mutters a "thanks" for the gesture and figures <<=_heOrShe>> isn't getting any more work done like this.
		<<switch $tmpGirl.location>>
		<<case 'quarry'>>
			<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> heads off toward the spring to rinse off, laughing under <<=_hisOrHer>> breath the whole way.
		<<case 'garden'>>
			<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> grabs the garden hose and rinses off right there, still grinning.
		<<case 'forest'>>
			<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> heads for the nearby stream to rinse off, shaking <<=_hisOrHer>> head at you the whole way.
		<</switch>>
		<br /><br />
		<div>
			<<link 'Leave'>>
				<<goto _backPassage>>
			<</link>>
			<div class="link-desc">Happiness +<<=_reactHappy>><<if _reactRel>> &bull; Relationship +<<=_reactRel>><</if>> &bull; Submission <<=(_reactSub >= 0 ? '+' : '') + _reactSub>><<=_goodwillPart>></div>
		</div>
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<set $tmpGirl.happy = Math.max($tmpGirl.happy - 3, -100)>>
	<<set $tmpGirl.relationship = Math.max($tmpGirl.relationship - 3, -100)>>
	<<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> doesn't find it funny at all. <<=ucfirst(_heOrShe)>> wipes <<=_himOrHer>>self off as best <<=_heOrShe>> can and goes back to work without a word, sticky and clearly unhappy about it.
	<br /><br />
	<div>
		<<link 'Leave'>>
			<<goto _backPassage>>
		<</link>>
		<div class="link-desc">Happiness -3 &bull; Relationship -3<<=_goodwillPart>></div>
	</div>
<</if>>
